#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -euo pipefail

usage() {
    cat <<'HELP'
Usage: pos-person add NAME
       pos-person identity PERSON SCOPE
       pos-person rename ID NAME
       pos-person wait TARGET PERSON [NOTE]
       pos-person arrived TARGET [STATE [NOTE]]
       pos-person --help

Record people, who each is in a scope, and which tasks wait on them,
in the ClankOS container.
"clankos-run help pos-person" prints the protocol.

    pos-person wait intray.org:12 'Ada Brook' 'Asked on Friday'
    intray.org:12: WAITING Ask Ada for the quote

add records a person once, as a file in person-entities/ of the root's
configuration directory. identity gives PERSON an identity in SCOPE, a
scope's path from the working directory, "." for the root. rename
gives the identity with ID a new NAME, in its file and in each link to
it. wait sets TARGET to WAITING and links it to PERSON's identity in
its scope, making one if there is none. arrived removes that link and
sets TARGET to STATE, NEXT when none is given.

PERSON is a recorded person's name, or their file's name without .org.
TARGET is the task's ID, or FILE:LINE, as pos-state takes it.

Exit: 0 saved, 2 usage, 255 refused or Emacs error, its message on
stderr; 125, 126 and 127 are clankos-run's.
HELP
}

case "${1:-}" in
    ''|help|-h|--help) usage; exit 0 ;;
esac
exec "$(cd -- "$(dirname -- "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")" && pwd)/clankos-run" pos-person "$@"
